{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings of length 12 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". Count sequences with no run of 3 same bits. Classic Fibonacci-like. For length n, number of binary strings with no 3 consecutive equal bits. Let a_n be count. Recurrence: a_n = a_{n-1} + a_{n-2}. Actually for no 3 consecutive equal bits, we can use DP with states: last run length and bit. Let's compute quickly.\n\nDefine dp[n][b][k] where last bit b (0/1) and run length k=1 or 2. For n=1: dp[1][0][1]=1, dp[1][1][1]=1. For n>1: transition: if add same bit, only if k=1 -> new k=2. if add different bit, new k=1. So recurrence.\n\nWe can compute total a_n = sum over b,k dp[n][b][k].\n\nLet's compute iteratively.\n\nn=1: totals: 2.\n\nn=2: compute:\nFrom dp[1][0][1]=1: add 0 -> k=2: dp[2][0][2]+=1. add 1 -> dp[2][1][1]+=1.\nFrom dp[1][1][1]=1: add 1 -> dp[2][1][2]+=1. add 0 -> dp[2][0][1]+=1.\nSo dp[2]:\n[0][1]=1\n[0][2]=1\n[1][1]=1\n[1][2]=1\nTotal 4.\n\nn=3:\nFrom each state:\ndp[2][0][1]=1: add 0 -> dp[3][0][2]+=1; add1 -> dp[3][1][1]+=1.\ndp[2][0][2]=1: can only add 1 -> dp[3][1][1]+=1 (since run length resets to1).\ndp[2][1][1]=1: add1 -> dp[3][1][2]+=1; add0 -> dp[3][0][1]+=1.\ndp[2][1][2]=1: add0 -> dp[3][0][1]+=1.\n\nCompute totals:\ndp[3][0][1] from two contributions: 1+1=2\ndp[3][0][2] =1\ndp[3][1][1] =1+1=2\ndp[3][1][2] =1\nTotal =2+1+2+1=6.\n\nn=4:\nStart with dp[3] values.\n\ndp[3][0][1]=2: add0 -> dp[4][0][2]+=2; add1 -> dp[4][1][1]+=2.\ndp[3][0][2]=1: add1 -> dp[4][1][1]+=1.\ndp[3][1][1]=2: add1 -> dp[4][1][2]+=2; add0 -> dp[4][0][1]+=2.\ndp[3][1][2]=1: add0 -> dp[4][0][1]+=1.\n\nCompute:\ndp[4][0][1] =2+1=3\ndp[4][0][2] =2\ndp[4][1][1] =2+1=3\ndp[4][1][2] =2\nTotal =3+2+3+2=10.\n\nn=5:\ndp[4] values.\n\ndp[4"}}],"created":1790946661,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","sy